--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Not in this repository, but shipped inside the Flatpak
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  /app/share/fonts/NotoSansTC-Regular.otf   OFL-1.1
      Noto Sans CJK, Subset OTF for Traditional Chinese, release Sans2.004,
      https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk
      Redistributed unmodified. It is in the package because the GNOME
      runtime ships no CJK font of any kind, and without one every translated
      line renders as empty boxes on a host that has none of its own. The
      subset rather than the full 15.7 MB face: measured against 1642 real
      translated lines it misses one character out of 1283.

      The rpm and deb do not contain it -- they are installed on a system
      whose own fonts are already there to be used.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Not in this repository: the models the program downloads
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

No installer built from this tree ships a model. The recogniser, translator
and punctuation models are fetched into ~/.cache/liveinterpreter/models/ and
are governed by their own licences, listed in assets/models.toml.

One of them needs saying out loud:

  NLLB-200-distilled-600M (the default translator)      CC-BY-NC-4.0

      Non-commercial. Running this program for yourself is fine. Building a
      product on it is not, and neither is redistributing the model. If you
      need a commercial translator, replace it -- the MT backend is behind a
      trait (crates/li-mt), and assets/models.toml is where the choice is
      recorded.

And one needs crediting:

  Opus-MT en-zh (the fallback translator)               CC-BY-4.0

      Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-en-zh, by Jörg Tiedemann and Santhosh
      Thottingal, "OPUS-MT -- Building open translation services for the
      World" (EAMT 2020), https://huggingface.co/Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-en-zh.
      Downloaded in a third-party CTranslate2 int8 conversion
      (jiangzhuo9357/opus-mt-en-zh-ct2), not modified further. Asked only for
      the pieces NLLB cannot write a character of.

The Apache-2.0 licence on this code does not extend to any of those models,
and none of them is a derivative work of this code.
